13
01:13:02,857 --> 01:13:08,857
Knight of Cups is a 2015 American romantic drama film
written and directed by Terrence Malick.

14
01:18:40,000 --> 01:18:46,000
Starring Christian Bale, Cate Blanchett, and Natalie Portman, film follows Rick (Bale), a hedonistic screenwriter who goes on an odyssey through Los Angeles and Las
Vegas as he undertakes a series of adventures with several people, including his ex-wife Nancy (Blanchett) and his married lover Elizabeth (Portman).

15
01:24:17,142 --> 01:24:23,142
The film is loosely inspired by, and at times quotes directly from, the 1678 Christian allegory The Pilgrim's
Progress, the Acts of Thomas passage "Hymn of the Pearl", and Suhrawardi's A Tale of the Western Exile.

16
01:29:54,285 --> 01:30:00,285
Each of the characters is identified by a tarot card from the Major
Arcana, with Bale representing the Knight of Cups.

17
01:35:31,428 --> 01:35:37,428
Knight of Cups premiered at the 65th Berlin International Film Festival on
February 8, 2015, where it was nominated for the Golden Bear.

18
01:41:08,571 --> 01:41:14,571
The film was theatrically released in the United States on March 4, 2016, to mixed reviews from critics, with
several finding the narrative structure incoherent, while others praised the visual style.

19
01:46:45,714 --> 01:46:51,714
The film explores themes of dreams, midlife crisis,
screenwriter, creative crisis, success.

20
01:52:22,857 --> 01:52:28,857
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
